        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buena_Vista%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 1900s the Vinton Colliery Company built 84 company houses and a blast furnace that produced 600 tons of pig iron annually.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/buena-vista-pennsylvania-ghost-town/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Each house in Buena Vista originally accommodated four families, one per corner.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://gaphistory.org/point_of_interest/buena-vista/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Great Depression turned Buena Vista into a ghost town, leaving behind crumbling foundations and abandoned mine openings.",
